  <div class="eyebrow">SHORT OBSERVATIONS</div><h1>Notes</h1><p class="lede">Small ideas worth keeping. These are working notes, not finished arguments.</p>
  <div class="entry"><div class="entry-date">DRAFT NOTE</div><div><h3>A system is more than its function</h3><p>Understanding a system requires looking beyond its intended function: constraints, failure modes and the environment matter too.</p></div></div>
  <div class="entry"><div class="entry-date">DRAFT NOTE</div><div><h3>Ask when it fails</h3><p>A useful engineering question is not only whether something works, but under what conditions it stops working.</p></div></div>
  <div class="entry"><div class="entry-date">DRAFT NOTE</div><div><h3>Research begins with a testable question</h3><p>Research becomes more concrete when a question can lead to an observation, a model or an experiment.</p></div></div>
